# Input
```ts
// should not generate diagnostics
// A `let` initialized with `null` takes the type of the value that the code
// assigns to it, as in TypeScript, so the left operand of the `||` below
// can't be nullish.

function assigned(input: string) {
	let label = null;
	label = input;
	return label || "none";
}

```
